{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: unreachable guard + duplicated parsing after the gh-N restriction**

Since the new `GITHUB_ISSUE_KEY` guard only passes keys of the exact shape `gh-N` (which always end in digits), the following check is now dead code:

```javascript
var num = extractIssueNumber(ticketKey);
if (!num) return body;
```

No key that reaches this point can yield `num === null`. The double `String(ticketKey || '').trim()` (once in the guard, once inside `extractIssueNumber`) is also redundant. This could be simplified to a single parse:

```javascript
var m = /^gh-(\d+)$/i.exec(String(ticketKey || '').trim());
if (!m) return body;
var num = m[1];
```

Not blocking — the current form is correct, just carries a small amount of now-unreachable defensive code.
